        after: "Kansas I'm leaving: predictable income, evenings off, only answering to one boss.\nTrouble I expect in the next 90 days: a client leaves, a Meta ad account gets restricted, a month with zero new signings.\nWeird alliances: a freelance editor, a VA, another agency I refer overflow to.\nRule: when I want to click my heels, I reread this list and make 10 prospecting calls before deciding anything.",
        body: "And for client ads: when ZDub runs a bolder PMT ad (“Afraid of motorcycles? Good. You're our favorite student.”), Zach warns PMT beforehand that a few people will comment angrily. That reaction is the tornado from the sidebar, and it means the ad is being noticed."
